  "notes": "The related noun {呪|のろ}い means 'curse.' This word appears frequently in horror, folklore, and fantasy contexts, but is also used figuratively to express deep resentment (e.g., cursing one's fate or bad luck).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {呪|のろ}いをかける — to cast a curse\n- {呪|のろ}いを{解|と}く — to break a curse\n- {運命|うんめい}を{呪|のろ}う — to curse one's fate\n- {呪|のろ}われた{場所|ばしょ} — cursed place\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {呪|のろ}い — curse (noun)\n- {呪文|じゅもん} — spell, incantation\n- {祟|たた}り — divine curse, retribution",
